solution.text:
According to de-Broglie. wavelength, $\lambda=\frac{h}{m v}$
Given, $\quad m=100 \mathrm{g}, v=100 \mathrm{cm} \mathrm{s}^{-1}$
and
$$
\begin{aligned}
h &=6.6 \times 10^{-34} \mathrm{J}-\mathrm{s} \\
&=6.6 \times 10^{-27} \mathrm{erg}-\mathrm{s}
\end{aligned}
$$
On substituting values, we get
$$
\lambda=\frac{6.6 \times 10^{-27}}{100 \times 100}=6.6 \times 10^{-31} \mathrm{cm}
$$
